    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.statusline\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nWhen opening a file that's inside of a large git repository, the git branch is not visible in the statusline until some action (e.g. scrolling, or pressing <kbd>:</kbd> or <kbd>j</kbd>), then it suddenly appears. I can't reproduce this with a blank `git init`-d repo, but I can if I clone a large public one (see reproduction steps).\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\nNVIM v0.9.1\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. `git clone` a large repo (e.g. `git clone git@github.com:Rapptz/discord.py.git`)\r\n2. Open a file in it with nvim (e.g. `nvim discord.py/setup.py`)\r\n3. Observe the status bar <img width=\"645\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/44343874/6a683a85-1972-48d5-96a0-a8af4915e7f3\">\r\n4. Press <kbd>j</kbd>\r\n5. Observe the status bar <img width=\"648\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/44343874/83a0b081-5127-4f44-b8d0-00e5f2f50e8f\">\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nStatus bar instantly has the git repo\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nStatus bar requires user action to show the git repo",
