            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for creating this!\r\n\r\nI can not reproduce. I've cloned that whole repository and after opening the file it indeed shows statusline without git section, but for a split second. After that, it automatically updates to show it.\r\n\r\nI am not sure why it isn't automatically updating in your case. It might be because 'lazy.nvim' (which you seem to be using) somehow affects plugin load or machine is not fast enough, or something else.\r\n\r\nThe reason the section appears after any movement is because they cause redraw of statusline which will show up to date information.\r\n\r\nI don't think this is an issue with 'mini.statusline' as it mostly defines 'statusline' option and not controls when it is updated. If this bothers you that much, you can try to manually redraw statusline on startup in your config:\r\n- `vim.cmd('redrawstatus!')` will redraw it immediately.\r\n- `vim.defer_fn(function() vim.cmd('redrawstatus!') end, 100)` will schedule to redraw it after 100 milliseconds.",
